The Fool the Lockout challenge in picoCTF 2026 is a Web Exploitation task that demonstrates how to bypass a poorly implemented IP-based rate limiter to perform a credential stuffing attack. 

🔍 Challenge Overview
The application implements a login rate limit to prevent brute-forcing:

Max Attempts: 10 failed logins. 
Time Window: 30 seconds (EPOCH_DURATION). 
Lockout Duration: 120 seconds.
The source code reveals a critical flaw in the refresh_request_rates_db function: it uses a fixed time window rather than a sliding window.  The counter resets to zero strictly when current_time - epoch_start > 30 seconds. 


